      "content": "wait, i'm so confused. you just said they have ketoacidosis, right? but then you're telling me to give them a snack? if their sugar is high enough to cause that, wouldn't more sugar be dangerous? they are literally gasping for air now and they're almost completely unresponsive. i'm terrified because you said to give them a snack but i feel like they're dying. should i just give them some insulin instead and hope they wake up? should i really just keep trying snacks and water or is this a life or death situation?",
